# bindings/ and samples/ are NOT ignored: the emitted artifacts are committed
# and CI regenerates them and fails on any diff, which is what stops anyone
# hand-editing one. A vendor building from a source tarball may have no Python.
#
# tests/reference/slice.json is NOT ignored: the goldens are committed, and a
# change to them has to show up in a diff like any other change to what this
# library is expected to send.

# Left behind only by an interrupted `make check-goldens`.
tests/reference/slice.json.committed
